      "content": "Hi, I'm currently reviewing some design proposals for an upcoming intersection upgrade in a busy part of London. We're weighing the pros and cons of sticking with a standard signalized intersection versus transitioning to a modern roundabout design.\n\nCould you give me a breakdown of how these two options typically compare regarding vehicle throughput and delay metrics? I'm especially interested in how they manage flow during peak hours and how much \"friction\" or unpredictable interruptions tend to impact the overall stability of each system.",
